  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The secondary structure of protein includes two type :</p><p>(a) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math>-Helix</p><p>(b) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#946;</mi></math>-pleated sheet</p><p>In <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math>-Helix structure, the poly peptide chain&nbsp;is coil around due to presence of Intramolecular <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math>-Bonding.</p>"
